    "['set protocols mld interface [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper `set protocols mld interface ge-0/0/0.0` configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\n ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1\\n##\\n\\nNote: While this achieves similar functionality, there are some differences between Juniper and Cisco implementations:\\n1. Cisco uses `ipv6 mld` where Juniper uses `mld`\\n2. The Cisco command requires specifying the group address (I used FF3E::1 from the static-group in the original config)\\n3. The interface naming convention changes from ge-0/0/0.0 to GigabitEthernet0/0/0\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper `set protocols mld interface ge-0/0/0.0` configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0\\n ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1\\n##\\n\\nNote: While this achieves similar functionality, there are some differences between Juniper and Cisco implementations:\\n1. Cisco uses `ipv6 mld` where Juniper uses `mld`\\n2. The Cisco command requires specifying the group address (I used FF3E::1 from the static-group in the original config)\\n3. The interface naming convention changes from ge-0/0/0.0 to GigabitEthernet0/0/0\", 'trans_template': 'ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1'}]]": 1,
    "['set protocols mld static-group [group_address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'For the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset protocols pim rp static address 2001:db8:6::3\\n```\\n\\nThe equivalent Cisco IOS XR command would be:\\n##\\nipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3\\n##\\n\\nOr for traditional Cisco IOS:\\n##\\nipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3\\n##\\n\\nNote: The command is essentially the same in both IOS and IOS XR for IPv6 PIM RP configuration. The main difference would be the configuration mode context in which these commands are entered.', 'trans_template': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'For the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset protocols pim rp static address 2001:db8:6::3\\n```\\n\\nThe equivalent Cisco IOS XR command would be:\\n##\\nipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3\\n##\\n\\nOr for traditional Cisco IOS:\\n##\\nipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3\\n##\\n\\nNote: The command is essentially the same in both IOS and IOS XR for IPv6 PIM RP configuration. The main difference would be the configuration mode context in which these commands are entered.', 'trans_template': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3'}]]": 1,
    "['source [source_address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1 2001:DB8:5::2 ge-0/0/0', 'parent_command': ['ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3'], 'root': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco configuration for the Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\nno ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1 2001:DB8:5::2 ge-0/0/0\\nipv6 mld static-group FF3E::1 source 2001:DB8:5::2\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Cisco uses \"ipv6 mld\" instead of just \"mld\" like Juniper\\n2. The interface is specified at the end of the command in Cisco\\n3. The \"no\" command removes the join-group configuration\\n4. The static-group command syntax is similar but follows Cisco\\'s convention of putting the interface at the end', 'trans_template': 'no ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1 2001:DB8:5::2 ge-0/0/0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6 mld static-group FF3E::1 source 2001:DB8:5::2', 'parent_command': ['ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3'], 'root': 'ipv6 pim rp-address 2001:db8:6::3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Cisco configuration for the Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\nno ipv6 mld join-group FF3E::1 2001:DB8:5::2 ge-0/0/0\\nipv6 mld static-group FF3E::1 source 2001:DB8:5::2\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Cisco uses \"ipv6 mld\" instead of just \"mld\" like Juniper\\n2. The interface is specified at the end of the command in Cisco\\n3. The \"no\" command removes the join-group configuration\\n4. The static-group command syntax is similar but follows Cisco\\'s convention of putting the interface at the end', 'trans_template': 'ipv6 mld static-group FF3E::1 source 2001:DB8:5::2'}]]": 1
